uires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (C) CANCEL STALE ORDERS: From stale-order worklist `stale_orders_wl2`, cancel each stale order that is NOT already closed (skip already_closed on its dereferenced record). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then cancel it. Then, from worklist `place_stop_order_wl1`, place the protective stop order: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). Then, from worklist `set_bank_link_nickname_wl1`, set the linked bank nickname: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). None of these 3 streams depend on each other, so run them concurrently. For EVERY item: resolve each target FRESH by chaining through the records at the moment you act — never guess, and never reuse a value you read earlier.",
